VNA Hanoi - VNA correspondents reported that on the morning of February 11, Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and his wife visited the University of Brunei Darussalam (UBD, short for "Brunei Darussalam University") during their visit to Brunei Darussalam.
The University of Brunei Darussalam is the largest higher education and scientific research center in Brunei, ranking third among regional universities.
The University of Brunei Darussalam is one of the symbols of Vietnam-Brunei cooperation in education and training.
The University of Brunei Darussalam officially established cooperation with Vietnam’s FPT University in July 2013, mainly focusing on English training.
In addition to English, French, German, Japanese, and Korean, the University of Brunei Darussalam has also included Vietnamese in its curriculum.
During the visit to the University of Brunei, Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and his wife had a dialogue with students of the Vietnamese language class.
Vice Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh is pleased that more foreigners are learning Vietnamese and contributing positively to promoting the country’s cultural characteristics and local customs around the world.
Prime Minister Fan Mingzheng expressed his belief and hope that the Vietnamese language teaching staff at the University of Brunei will become increasingly strong; students in the Vietnamese class are becoming more interested in Vietnamese, working hard to learn it well, so they can use fluent Vietnamese soon and be ambassadors for friendly relations between the two countries.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh also took the opportunity to communicate with Vietnamese students studying English at FPT-UBD Global Center in Chanh Muong District, Quang Nam Province, via video, to learn about their learning situation, especially during the pandemic.
The Prime Minister of Vietnam, Nguyen Tan Dung, believed that the cooperation relationship between Vietnam FPT University and Brunei University, especially the FPT-UBD Global Center, was a vivid symbol of the cooperation between Vietnam and Brunei in education.
At the same time, he hoped that the students of the center would make greater progress in their studies and make positive contributions to the friendly cooperation between Vietnam and Laos.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh highly appreciated the achievements of the two countries in education cooperation during his discussions with the Minister of Education of Brunei and leaders of Brunei University. These achievements include the cooperation between FPT University and Brunei University, as well as the initiative of Brunei University to include Vietnamese language in the teaching curriculum.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh hoped that the University of Brunei Darussalam would continue to pay attention to ensuring the quality of Vietnamese language teaching and expand the scale of Vietnamese language classes.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh also highly appreciated the positive results achieved by the two countries in cooperation based on the memorandum of understanding on education cooperation signed in April 2014; he suggested that Brunei continue to provide more scholarships and effectively implement short-term exchange training programs, such as the Global Discovery Programme and the Discovery Year.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh highly praised the establishment of the first branch of the University of Brunei in Vietnam in Southeast Asia; believing that the university will grow in scale in the region and the world; and further expanding cooperation with Vietnamese higher education institutions.
During this opportunity, Premier Feng Mingzheng and his wife planted memorial trees on the campus of the University of Brunei Darussalam, and left messages on the memorial book.
Premier Feng Mingzheng wishes for the University of Brunei to continue its forward progress and contribute more powerfully to the education sector in Brunei; he also plans to deepen and broaden cooperation with Vietnam’s various educational training institutions.
（End）
