Worst online shopping experience
After placing the order on September 28, the system showed that the goods had been shipped, but I did not receive the goods until October 12.
Query Amazon order status; seller did not provide shipping label, so cannot find where the order is.
So I sent an email to the seller asking if they could provide me with the shipping number, but I didn't get a reply for two days.
In desperation, I called Amazon customer service and they told me the seller's phone number. After calling the store again several times, the line was connected and I was informed that the package had been lost. They said I could immediately have another one sent to me.
Although I was particularly angry, I didn't say much to the seller because I urgently needed the computer. I just wanted to send it to me as soon as possible.
The result is that I called the next day to ask if the shipment had been sent.
The seller said it hasn't arrived yet and it will be sent in the afternoon.
I called again this afternoon to ask, but the seller said it would definitely be sent; they promised to ship after 5 or 6 PM in the afternoon. However, when I called at 7 PM, no one answered the phone.
The next morning, I called again to check if the goods had been shipped.
Can you tell me the order number?
The seller said it was not sent, and told me to order from another store if I was in a hurry, or it would be sent in the afternoon if I could wait.
There’s no way, I have to wait for a long time to order from other places.
I can only ask the seller to send the goods as soon as possible.
Finally, after countless phone follow-ups, I received the computer on October 16th.
As for the quality of the computer, I don't know because it was bought for someone else, so I will add a comment later.
